## Why This Is Asked
Tests a non-Kinesis ingest path, queue-based decoupling, and traceability end-to-end. It also checks idempotent dedupe, effective error handling, and end-to-end testing in LocalStack.

## Key Concepts
- API Gateway to SQS producer path
- SQS DLQ handling
- DynamoDB upsert for per-device dedupe
- S3 Parquet writes partitioned by date
- X-Ray trace propagation across services
- LocalStack end-to-end testing

## Code Example
```javascript
// Lambda: processFromSQS.js
exports.handler = async (event) => {
  for (const rec of event.Records) {
    const payload = JSON.parse(rec.body);
    // validate, score, write to DynamoDB/S3 as appropriate
  }
};
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you ensure at-least-once vs exactly-once semantics?
- How would you handle out-of-order events per device?
- What metrics would you surface to CloudWatch for this pipeline?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests cross-region, multi-tenant streaming with privacy, exactly-once semantics, observability, and governance.

## Key Concepts
- Tenant isolation and partitioning
- Ingestion-time PII redaction
- Idempotent processing and deduplication
- End-to-end tracing (OpenTelemetry/X-Ray)
- Data lifecycle: TTL and backfill

## Code Example
